    {
      "id": "box-mesh-cave-contacts",
      "kind": "micro",
      "description": "Box/triangle-mesh contacts for 64 boxes (half extents 0.4 x 0.3 x 0.5) resting on a closed 1968-triangle cave floor, axis aligned and tilted, 0.02 margin.",
      "dimensions": {
        "boxes": 64,
        "triangles": 1968,
        "poses": "resting,tilted"
      },
      "correctnessEvidence": [
        "crates/geometry-kernels/benches/performance_smoke.rs::box_mesh_contacts (cave_resting_64, cave_tilted_64)",
        "crates/geometry-kernels/tests/box_mesh_manifold.rs"
      ],
      "metrics": [
        {
          "name": "callgrind-ir",
          "unit": "instructions",
          "direction": "lower",
          "signal": "instruction-count",
          "blocking": true,
          "budget": {
            "relativeRegressionPercent": 5
          },
          "notes": "Guards rust-kernels#225 after #231 removed its three changes without a measurable effect (box-face axis shortcut, lazy inward normals, branch-free best-axis select). What remains (plain loops instead of iterator chains, structure-of-arrays edge axes, two-buffer polygon clipping, iterative BVH walk) is bit-identical to the pre-#225 kernel and measured 0.71-0.83 of its wall time in an interleaved A/B; instructions are about equal (2.77M/2.05M resting/tilted vs 2.76M/2.11M), so the gain comes from vectorization and code generation callgrind does not model; end to end in physics-engine it was within noise. Benchmark ids were renamed in #231 to re-seed: earlier runs undercounted, because a closure defined inside the benchmark function made the kernel's symbol match Iai-Callgrind's collection toggle. Keep measured loops in module-level helpers. Also guards the follow-up that inlines contacts() into the mesh walk, writes the per-triangle frame transforms and projections as explicit arrays (nested array maps compiled to out-of-line try_map instances) and inlines closest_segment_points and math3::is_finite: bit-identical, 2.53M/1.76M instructions resting/tilted (from 2.74M/2.02M), native wall time 0.66-0.87 of 593b133 in the interleaved A/B; measured for physics-engine redbrand-rigid-mesh."
        }
      ]
    },
